IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `or336-nouns`

-- Art. 336b of the Swiss Code of Obligations (OR, SR 220), Fedlex consolidated
-- version applicable from 2026-10-01: procedure (Verfahren): the written
-- objection (Einsprache) against the notice, then the action, and the
-- forfeiture of the claim (verwirkt).
--
-- LAYER 1, MODULE 4. Objective: it takes nobody's point of view. "Wer ... eine
-- Entschädigung geltend machen will" is the party that RECEIVED the notice
-- (the compensation is owed to "die andere Partei", Art. 336a(1)), and
-- "der Kündigende" is the party that gave it.
--
-- Dates are `Date day month year`. The two periods of the text are the end
-- of the notice period (an input: the notice period itself is not in the
-- encoded text) and 180 days after the end of the employment (the day the
-- employment ends is an input). Both are tested on the day before, the day
-- of and the day after (or336-tests-art336b.l4).
--
-- What a "no" and a "not covered" mean here: see the header of
-- or336-art336.l4 and NOTES.md.

§ `Art 336b -- procedure: the objection and the action`

§§ `Art 336b(1): the written objection, at the latest by the end of the notice period`

-- Art. 336b(1): the last day on which the objection can be made is the end of
-- the notice period ("längstens bis zum Ende der Kündigungsfrist"). The day is
-- taken as inclusive (fork F19 in NOTES.md).
-- src:40 | 1 Wer gestützt auf Artikel 336 und 336a eine Entschädigung geltend machen will, muss gegen die Kündigung längstens bis zum Ende der Kündigungsfrist beim Kündigenden schriftlich Einsprache erheben.
@ref Art 336b(1) (src:40)
GIVEN `the last day of the notice period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`Art 336b(1) the last day to object` MEANS
    `the last day of the notice period`

-- Art. 336b(1): whoever wants to assert a compensation under Art. 336 and
-- 336a must object to the notice, in writing, with the party that gave it,
-- at the latest by the end of the notice period. "Muss" is read as the text's
-- own requirement: an objection that is not in writing, not against the
-- notice, not made to the party that gave it, or made after the last day, does
-- not meet it (fork F20 in NOTES.md).
-- src:40 | 1 Wer gestützt auf Artikel 336 und 336a eine Entschädigung geltend machen will, muss gegen die Kündigung längstens bis zum Ende der Kündigungsfrist beim Kündigenden schriftlich Einsprache erheben.
@ref Art 336b(1) (src:40)
GIVEN objection IS AN `Objection`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 336b(1) the objection meets the requirements` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Wer gestützt auf Artikel 336 und 336a eine Entschädigung geltend machen will"
        IF NOT (objection's `the claim rests on Art 336 and 336a`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "muss ... schriftlich Einsprache erheben"
        IF NOT (objection's `the objection was made in writing`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "muss gegen die Kündigung ... Einsprache erheben"
        IF NOT (objection's `the objection was directed against the notice`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "muss ... beim Kündigenden schriftlich Einsprache erheben"
        IF NOT (objection's `the objection was made to the party that gave the notice`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "längstens bis zum Ende der Kündigungsfrist" (a period the text fixes: outside it, no)
        IF objection's `the day the objection was made` GREATER THAN `Art 336b(1) the last day to object` (objection's `the last day of the notice period`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The same provision as a regulative rule. The party that received the notice
-- MUST object in writing, WITHIN the days from the day the notice was given to
-- the end of the notice period. The clock starts on the day the notice was
-- given (an assumption, fork F26: the text names no start); the unit is DAYS.
-- The text states no sanction in paragraph 1; the BREACH stands for "the
-- condition for asserting the claim is not met" (paragraph 2 lets the claim be
-- asserted only after a valid objection) and is not a wrong in the ordinary
-- sense (fork F28 in NOTES.md).
-- src:40 | 1 Wer gestützt auf Artikel 336 und 336a eine Entschädigung geltend machen will, muss gegen die Kündigung längstens bis zum Ende der Kündigungsfrist beim Kündigenden schriftlich Einsprache erheben.
@ref Art 336b(1) (src:40)
GIVEN `the party that received the notice` IS A Party
      `the days from the notice to the end of the notice period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under Art 336 to 336b`
`Art 336b(1) the duty to object` MEANS
    PARTY `the party that received the notice`
    MUST `object in writing to the notice`
    WITHIN `the days from the notice to the end of the notice period`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "no objection in writing was made by the end of the notice period (Art. 336b(1)), so the compensation cannot be asserted"

§§ `Art 336b(2): assert the claim, and bring the action within 180 days`

-- Art. 336b(2), first sentence: if the objection was valid and the parties do
-- not agree on continuing the employment, the party that received the notice
-- can assert the compensation claim. A failed objection requirement is a no
-- (the flat "muss" of paragraph 1); an agreement to continue fails the
-- "wenn"-gate of a power, which is NOTHING (fork F21 in NOTES.md).
-- src:41 | 2 Ist die Einsprache gültig erfolgt und einigen sich die Parteien nicht über die Fortsetzung des Arbeitsverhältnisses, so kann die Partei, der gekündigt worden ist, ihren Anspruch auf Entschädigung geltend machen. Wird nicht innert 180 Tagen nach Beendigung des Arbeitsverhältnisses eine Klage anhängig gemacht, ist der Anspruch verwirkt.
@ref Art 336b(2) (src:41)
GIVEN `the objection meets the requirements of Art 336b(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the parties agreed on continuing the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 336b(2) the party that received the notice can assert the compensation claim` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "muss gegen die Kündigung ... Einsprache erheben" (Art. 336b(1): without a valid objection the claim cannot be asserted)
        IF `the objection meets the requirements of Art 336b(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Wer gestützt auf Artikel 336 und 336a eine Entschädigung geltend machen will" (the objection requirement is not decided on these facts)
        IF `the objection meets the requirements of Art 336b(1)` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Ist die Einsprache gültig erfolgt und einigen sich die Parteien nicht über die Fortsetzung des Arbeitsverhältnisses, so kann die Partei, der gekündigt worden ist, ihren Anspruch auf Entschädigung geltend machen" (a power gated by "wenn"; the text does not say that the power exists only if the parties do not agree)
        IF `the parties agreed on continuing the employment`
        THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Art. 336b(2), second sentence: the last day on which an action has to be
-- made pending is 180 days after the end of the employment. The day the
-- employment ended is day 0, so the last day is that day plus 180 (fork F22).
-- src:41 | 2 Ist die Einsprache gültig erfolgt und einigen sich die Parteien nicht über die Fortsetzung des Arbeitsverhältnisses, so kann die Partei, der gekündigt worden ist, ihren Anspruch auf Entschädigung geltend machen. Wird nicht innert 180 Tagen nach Beendigung des Arbeitsverhältnisses eine Klage anhängig gemacht, ist der Anspruch verwirkt.
@ref Art 336b(2) (src:41)
GIVEN `the day the employment ended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`Art 336b(2) the last day to bring the action` MEANS
    `the day the employment ended` PLUS 180

-- Art. 336b(2), second sentence: "Wird nicht innert 180 Tagen nach Beendigung
-- des Arbeitsverhältnisses eine Klage anhängig gemacht, ist der Anspruch
-- verwirkt." JUST TRUE: the claim is forfeited. JUST FALSE: it is not
-- (an action was made pending in time, or the 180 days have not yet run on the
-- day asked about). An action made pending before the employment ended counts
-- as in time (fork F23).
-- src:41 | 2 Ist die Einsprache gültig erfolgt und einigen sich die Parteien nicht über die Fortsetzung des Arbeitsverhältnisses, so kann die Partei, der gekündigt worden ist, ihren Anspruch auf Entschädigung geltend machen. Wird nicht innert 180 Tagen nach Beendigung des Arbeitsverhältnisses eine Klage anhängig gemacht, ist der Anspruch verwirkt.
@ref Art 336b(2) (src:41)
GIVEN action IS AN `Action on the claim`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 336b(2) the claim is forfeited` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF action's `an action has been brought` AND `the action was brought in time`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Wird nicht innert 180 Tagen nach Beendigung des Arbeitsverhältnisses eine Klage anhängig gemacht, ist der Anspruch verwirkt" (an action was made pending within the 180 days: the "wenn" of the forfeiture is not met)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        IF action's `an action has been brought`
        -- the action was made pending after the last day: no action within 180 days
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the day asked about` AT MOST `the last day to bring the action`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "innert 180 Tagen nach Beendigung des Arbeitsverhältnisses" (no action yet, and the 180 days have not run out on the day asked about)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- no action was made pending and the 180 days had run out on the day asked about
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the last day to bring the action` MEANS
            `Art 336b(2) the last day to bring the action` (action's `the day the employment ended`)
        `the day asked about` MEANS action's `the day asked about`
        `the action was brought in time` MEANS
            action's `the day the action was brought` AT MOST `the last day to bring the action`

-- The same sentence as a regulative rule. The party that received the notice
-- MAY make an action pending WITHIN 180 days after the end of the employment
-- (clock day 0 = the day the employment ended; unit = days). The text states a
-- consequence of letting the 180 days pass: the claim is forfeited. DO is the
-- optionality modal: HENCE when the act is done in time, LEST when the days
-- pass. A MAY with a LEST is read differently on the stable binary (the
-- lapse is FULFILLED); DO carries both branches and imposes no duty to sue
-- (fork F28 in NOTES.md).
-- src:41 | 2 Ist die Einsprache gültig erfolgt und einigen sich die Parteien nicht über die Fortsetzung des Arbeitsverhältnisses, so kann die Partei, der gekündigt worden ist, ihren Anspruch auf Entschädigung geltend machen. Wird nicht innert 180 Tagen nach Beendigung des Arbeitsverhältnisses eine Klage anhängig gemacht, ist der Anspruch verwirkt.
@ref Art 336b(2) (src:41)
GIVEN `the party that received the notice` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under Art 336 to 336b`
`Art 336b(2) the window to bring the action` MEANS
    PARTY `the party that received the notice`
    DO `bring an action`
    WITHIN 180
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "no action was made pending within 180 days after the end of the employment, so the claim is forfeited (Art. 336b(2))"
